-- ex35 reshape row: a vector of soldiers into 4 rows, the trailing axis computed. Twin of 064-two-habitats.bqn.
-- The reshape row: eight soldiers into four ranks, to 4 _ computing the rest.
-- Eight soldiers; pos = to 4 _ mints exactly count-of-selection positions as the ravel of ↕4‿2: soldier k gets cell (k div 2, k mod 2), the coordinate form of the .bqn's 4‿∘⥊↕8 with the trailing axis computed as 8/4 = 2.
-- pos starts as -1 -1 junk pairs to prove the full overwrite; expect compares the flattened pair column.
--! registry ../registries/067-two-habitats-d.reg
--! expect-n 8
--! expect pos = 0 0 0 1 1 0 1 1 2 0 2 1 3 0 3 1

Soldier , pos = to 4 _
